# fika-sync/gui/.env — APPLICATION credentials (a one-time setup,
# done by whoever runs this GUI, not by each person who uses it
# afterward).
#
# SIMPLER ALTERNATIVE TO THIS FILE: paste these same credentials
# directly into the "Connections" tab of the GUI, in the amber "App
# configuration" card — no need to restart the server or touch any
# file. This .env still works the same way if you prefer that route
# (for example, to automate deployment); what's saved from the GUI
# takes priority over these variables if both are present.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" in this same folder and fill it in. It's
# loaded automatically when `python3 app.py` starts (see app.py,
# load_dotenv). Never commit the real .env with actual credentials —
# ".env" is already in .gitignore if the repo includes it; if not,
# add it before pasting anything here.
#
# Cal.com does NOT go here, ever: each person connects THEIR OWN
# key from their row in the "Team" tab (recommended — see
# fika-sync/gui/README.md, "Why Cal.com is also a per-person
# connection" section), or alternatively someone pastes a shared key
# in the "Connections" tab (only gives correct data for the whole
# team if it's a key from a paid Cal.com Team plan). Neither path
# touches this file.

# --- Google (Calendar + Sheets) ---------------------------------
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# 2. Create a project (or use an existing one) and enable the
#    "Google Calendar API" and "Google Sheets API"
#    (https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library).
# 3. "Create credentials" -> "OAuth client ID" -> application type
#    "Web application" (NOT "Desktop app" — that's the manual flow
#    in VALIDATION.md, different from this one).
# 4. Under "Authorized redirect URIs" add EXACTLY:
#      http://127.0.0.1:5000/oauth/google/callback
#    (or the real domain if this isn't running on localhost — it has
#    to match character for character what the GUI generates).
# 5. Copy the "Client ID" and "Client Secret" below.
# 6. On the "OAuth consent screen", if the project is in "Testing"
#    mode, add every Google account that's going to connect as a
#    "Test user" — Google blocks login for any account not on that
#    list while the project isn't published.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Slack ---------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Go to https://api.slack.com/apps -> "Create New App" -> "From
#    scratch".
# 2. "OAuth & Permissions" (left menu):
#    - Under "Redirect URLs" add EXACTLY:
#        http://127.0.0.1:5000/oauth/slack/callback
#    - Under "Scopes" -> "Bot Token Scopes" add "chat:write".
# 3. "Basic Information" -> "App Credentials": copy the "Client ID"
#    and "Client Secret" below.
# 4. "Manage Distribution" -> complete the checklist -> "Activate
#    Public Distribution". WITHOUT THIS STEP, the GUI's "Connect
#    Slack" button only works for the workspace where the app was
#    created — it's not a bug, Slack blocks it that way by design.
#    Doesn't require Slack to review anything, it's self-service.
SLACK_CLIENT_ID=
SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Alternative: full variables instead of the "connect with one
# click" flow (not recommended if you're going to use the GUI, but
# still works) -----------------------------------------------------
# See fika-sync/.env.example for GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN, SLACK_BOT_TOKEN
# and CALCOM_API_KEY generated by hand — VALIDATION.md explains how to
# get them. If you'd rather paste Cal.com's API key from the
# "Connections" tab, there's no need to touch anything here for
# Cal.com in either case.
